{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_017wtnKK7LKC2np8ZFqUHe9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q12: Budget estimate for RAG at enterprise scale (e.g. 300K legal contracts)**:\n\n---\n\n**Three-phase cost model:**\n\n| Phase | Cost |\n|-------|------|\n| **Ingestion (one-time)** | ~$7,500 — dominated by PDF extraction (Textract: $6,750 for 4.5M scanned pages; native PyMuPDF: ~$0) + embedding generation ($34 at text-embedding-3-small) |\n| **Storage (monthly)** | ~$150–$350 — Pinecone $70/month or self-hosted Qdrant $250/month (HA) for 1.7M vectors; S3 $23/month for 1TB PDFs |\n| **Serving (monthly)** | ~$600 at 5K queries/day — $0.004/query blended with 80% GPT-4o-mini / 20% GPT-4o model tiering |\n| **Total steady-state** | ~$900–$1,150/month + ~$7,500 one-time |\n\n**Key levers called out:**\n- Native PDF vs. Textract extraction changes upfront cost by ~$6,000\n- Model tiering is a 5–10× serving cost lever\n- Data-residency requirements (GDPR for legal corpus) may push self-hosted Qdrant despite higher infra cost\n\n**Pitfalls flagged:** Quoting only generation costs (ignoring ingestion), assuming all GPT-4o (no tiering), and hand-waving storage costs without numbers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":73769,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":308,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6b8d39-8884-4ea8-a82d-7a2a74a8e291","uuid":"cd5fa602-8d5a-41af-9df4-1961bc670b6a"}
